{"course": {"id": "s17", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics — Stage 7", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "Integers"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Expressions, Formulae and Equations"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Place Value and Rounding"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Decimals"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Angles and Constructions"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Collecting Data"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Shapes and Symmetry"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Sequences and Functions"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Percentages"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Graphs"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Position and Transformation"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Shapes, Area and Volume"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Interpreting and Discussing Results"}]}, "unit": {"n": 3, "stage": 17, "title": "Place Value and Rounding", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Multiplying and dividing whole numbers and decimals by 10, 100 and 1000, and rounding to the nearest power of 10 and to decimal places.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Lower Secondary Mathematics (0862), Stage 7", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m7u03.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "7Np.01", "sec": "3.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Multiply and divide integers and decimals by 10, 100 and 1000, using place value."}, "O2": {"code": "7Np.02", "sec": "3.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Round numbers to the nearest 10, 100 or 1000 and to a given number of decimal places."}}, "sections": [{"id": "3.1", "title": "Multiplying and dividing by powers of 10", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "A tiny screw", "p": ["A factory packs **1000 screws** in a box. Each screw has a mass of **2.35 g**.", "What is the mass of one box of screws? And if one screw is 2.35 g, what is the mass of a tenth of it? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Place value", "p": ["In 4.07 the 4 is worth 4 ones, the 0 is worth 0 tenths and the 7 is worth 7 hundredths."], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s1t01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "What is the value of the digit 6 in 31.86?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "Count places after the decimal point.", "reason": "6 hundredths (0.06).", "options": [{"t": "6 hundredths", "ok": true, "fb": "It is in the second place after the point."}, {"t": "6 tenths", "ok": false, "fb": "The tenths digit is 8."}, {"t": "6 ones", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "6 thousandths", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Powers of 10", "p": ["10, 100, 1000, 10 000 … are all **powers of 10**. We can write them with an **index** (a small raised number) that tells you how many 10s are multiplied together:"], "table": {"head": ["Number", "Product of 10s", "Power of 10"], "rows": [["10", "10", "10¹"], ["100", "10 × 10", "10²"], ["1000", "10 × 10 × 10", "10³"], ["10 000", "10 × 10 × 10 × 10", "10⁴"]]}, "p2": ["The index is also the number of zeros after the 1: 10⁴ = 10 000 has four zeros."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Digits move, the point stays", "p": ["When you multiply by 10, every digit moves **one place to the left**, so it is worth 10 times as much. Dividing by 10 moves every digit **one place to the right**."], "table": {"head": ["", "H", "T", "O", ".", "t", "h", "th"], "rows": [["2.35", "", "", "2", ".", "3", "5", ""], ["2.35 × 10", "", "2", "3", ".", "5", "", ""], ["2.35 × 100", "2", "3", "5", ".", "", "", ""], ["2.35 ÷ 10", "", "", "0", ".", "2", "3", "5"]]}, "p2": ["× 10² (100) moves the digits 2 places left; ÷ 10³ (1000) moves them 3 places right.", "Fill empty places between the digits and the point with **zeros**: 4.6 × 1000 = 4600, 7 ÷ 100 = 0.07."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Multiply", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.48 × 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 48, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 4.8, "fb": "That is × 10. 100 = 10², so move 2 places."}], "bare": true, "hint": "Move each digit 2 places to the left.", "reason": "0.48 × 100 = 48."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I multiply or divide by a power of 10?", "p": ["Step 1: Count the zeros (or read the index): 10³ means 3 places.", "Step 2: × → digits move LEFT (the number gets bigger). ÷ → digits move RIGHT (the number gets smaller).", "Step 3: Fill gaps with zeros; leave off zeros at the end after the point (2.50 → 2.5).", "Step 4: Check the size: × should give a bigger answer, ÷ a smaller one."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Multiplying a decimal", "p": [], "q": "Work out 0.073 × 10³.", "steps": [["10³ = 1000, so move 3 places left", "the index is 3"], ["0.073 → 0.73 → 7.3 → 73", "one place at a time"], ["73", ""]], "a": "73", "check": "0.073 is about 0.07; 0.07 × 1000 = 70, and 73 is close. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Dividing a whole number", "p": [], "q": "Work out 56 ÷ 1000.", "steps": [["1000 = 10³: move 3 places right", ""], ["56 → 5.6 → 0.56 → 0.056", ""], ["0.056", "a zero fills the tenths place"]], "a": "0.056", "check": "0.056 × 1000 = 56. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Finding the missing power", "p": [], "q": "Fill the gap: 9.2 × ☐ = 920.", "steps": [["9.2 → 920: the 9 moved from ones to hundreds", "2 places left"], ["2 places = 10² = 100", ""]], "a": "100 (10²)", "check": "9.2 × 100 = 920. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "A real-life calculation", "p": [], "q": "A sheet of paper is 0.09 mm thick. How thick is a pile of 1000 sheets? Give your answer in cm.", "steps": [["0.09 × 1000 = 90 mm", "3 places left"], ["90 ÷ 10 = 9 cm", "10 mm = 1 cm"]], "a": "9 cm", "check": "A real ream of 500 sheets is about 5 cm thick, so 9 cm for 1000 is sensible. ✓"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Divide", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s1t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 3.4 ÷ 10².", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.034, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 0.34, "fb": "That is ÷ 10. Move 2 places."}, {"v": 340, "fb": "Dividing makes the number smaller."}], "bare": true, "hint": "10² = 100: move 2 places right.", "reason": "3.4 → 0.34 → 0.034."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Adding a zero", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Work out 6.8 × 10.", "lines": ["× 10 means add a zero", "6.8 × 10 = 6.80", "So the answer is 6.80"], "bad": 0, "why": "'Add a zero' only works for whole numbers. 6.80 is the same as 6.8 – nothing changed. The digits must move one place left.", "fix": [["6.8 × 10: digits move 1 place left", ""], ["= 68", ""]], "id": "m7u03s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "'Add a zero' for decimals", "p": ["Never 'add zeros' to multiply a decimal: move the digits. 3.5 × 100 = 350, not 3.500."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real-life powers of 10", "p": ["1 km = 1000 m, 1 m = 100 cm, 1 kg = 1000 g. Converting units is multiplying or dividing by a power of 10."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["10¹ = 10, 10² = 100, 10³ = 1000, 10⁴ = 10 000: the index is the number of zeros.", "× 10ⁿ: digits move n places left. ÷ 10ⁿ: digits move n places right.", "Fill gaps with zeros; the decimal point does not move.", "Check: multiplying makes it bigger, dividing makes it smaller."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 840, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "3.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m7u03s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: what is the mass of 1000 screws of 2.35 g each (in grams)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2350, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 235, "fb": "That is × 100."}], "bare": true, "hint": "Each digit moves 3 places left.", "reason": "2.35 × 1000 = 2350 g."}}, {"id": "3.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m7u03s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 7.1 × 10³.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7100, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 710, "fb": "10³ is 1000."}], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7100."}}, {"id": "3.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m7u03s1k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 85 ÷ 10⁴.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.0085, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 0.085, "fb": "That is ÷ 1000."}], "bare": true, "hint": "Move 4 places right.", "reason": "0.0085."}}, {"id": "3.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m7u03s1k04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Quick check: which is equal to 0.6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "Work out each.", "reason": "60 ÷ 100 = 0.6.", "options": [{"t": "60 ÷ 100", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "6 ÷ 100", "ok": false, "fb": "That is 0.06."}, {"t": "0.06 × 100", "ok": false, "fb": "That is 6."}, {"t": "600 ÷ 10", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 337]], "req": [{"id": "m7u03s1r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 4.2 × 10.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 42, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "42."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.35 × 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 35, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "35."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 1.9 × 1000.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1900, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "1900."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 74 ÷ 10.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7.4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7.4."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 6 ÷ 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.06, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 0.6, "fb": "That is ÷ 10."}], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.06."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 2.5 ÷ 10³.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.0025, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.0025."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Write 10⁴ as an ordinary number.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 40, "fb": "10⁴ is 10 × 10 × 10 × 10, not 10 × 4."}], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "10 000."}, {"id": "m7u03s1r08", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Fill the gap: 0.67 × ☐ = 67.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "100.", "options": [{"t": "100", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "10", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": "1000", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "prac": [{"id": "m7u03s1p01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.004 × 10⁴.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 40, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "40."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 307 ÷ 10³.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.307, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.307."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Fill the gap: 48 ÷ ☐ = 0.048. Give the power of 10 as a number.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1000, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "How many places did the digits move?", "reason": "3 places: 1000."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p04", "type": "num", "prompt": "A bag of rice has a mass of 2.4 kg. What is this in grams?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2400, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "1 kg = 1000 g.", "reason": "2400 g."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p05", "type": "num", "prompt": "A coin is 1.85 mm thick. How tall is a stack of 100 coins, in cm?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Problem solving", "answer": 18.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "185 mm, then ÷ 10.", "reason": "18.5 cm."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p06", "type": "grid", "prompt": "Bigger or smaller than the start number?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "cols": ["bigger", "smaller"], "rows": [{"l": "3.2 × 100", "a": ["bigger"]}, {"l": "3.2 ÷ 10", "a": ["smaller"]}, {"l": "0.5 × 10³", "a": ["bigger"]}, {"l": "500 ÷ 10²", "a": ["smaller"]}], "mode": "classify", "hint": "", "reason": "× makes bigger, ÷ makes smaller."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p07", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Max says 0.3 × 100 = 0.300. Explain his mistake and give the right answer.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "adding zeros to a decimal doesn't change it", "kw": ["zero|same|doesn.?t change|0\\.3"]}, {"pt": "digits move 2 places left", "kw": ["move|place|left"]}, {"pt": "answer 30", "kw": ["\\b30\\b"]}], "need": 2, "model": "0.300 is still 0.3: adding zeros after a decimal changes nothing. Multiplying by 100 moves the digits 2 places left: 0.3 × 100 = 30.", "hint": "", "reason": "0.300 is still 0.3: adding zeros after a decimal changes nothing. Multiplying by 100 moves the digits 2 places left: 0.3 × 100 = 30."}, {"id": "m7u03s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "A $1000 prize is shared equally by 100 people. How much does each get (in $)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "$10."}], "adv": [{"id": "m7u03s1a01", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Work out 0.52 × 10³ ÷ 10².", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5.2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "× 1000 then ÷ 100: overall × 10.", "reason": "5.2."}, {"id": "m7u03s1a02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "* Advanced. Which is the odd one out?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "Work out each one.", "reason": "0.07 × 10³ = 70.", "options": [{"t": "0.07 × 10³", "ok": true, "fb": "This is 70; the others are 7."}, {"t": "700 ÷ 10²", "ok": false, "fb": "7"}, {"t": "0.7 × 10", "ok": false, "fb": "7"}, {"t": "7000 ÷ 10³", "ok": false, "fb": "7"}]}, {"id": "m7u03s1a03", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. Light travels about 300 000 km each second. Write 300 000 as 3 × 10ⁿ. What is n?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Count the zeros.", "reason": "3 × 10⁵."}], "more": [{"id": "m7u03s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 5.6 × 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 560, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "560."}, {"id": "m7u03s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.09 × 10.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.9."}, {"id": "m7u03s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 820 ÷ 100.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 8.2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "8.2."}, {"id": "m7u03s1m04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 3 ÷ 1000.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.003, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "0.003."}, {"id": "m7u03s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Work out 0.016 × 10².", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1.6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "1.6."}, {"id": "m7u03s1m06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Change 450 cm to metres.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "÷ 100", "reason": "4.5 m."}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c7u03", "p0": 2, "p1": 6, "label": "pages 2–6", "title": "Lesson 3.1 notes · Multiplying and dividing by powers of 10", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "3.2", "title": "Rounding", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "How fast?", "p": ["A sprinter's time is shown on a big screen as **10.4 s**, but the timing system measured **10.386 s**.", "Why does the screen not show every digit? What would it show with two digits after the point? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Rounding whole numbers", "p": ["To round 3748 to the nearest hundred: it lies between 3700 and 3800; the tens digit is 4 (less than 5), so it rounds down to 3700."], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 6251 to the nearest hundred.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6300, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 6200, "fb": "5 or more rounds up."}, {"v": 6250, "fb": "That is the nearest ten."}], "bare": true, "hint": "Look at the tens digit.", "reason": "Tens digit 5 → round up: 6300."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Degree of accuracy", "p": ["You are always told how accurate the rounded number must be – this is the **degree of accuracy**: nearest whole number, 1 decimal place (1 d.p.), 2 d.p. and so on.", "The rule is the same every time:"], "table": {"head": ["Step", "What to do"], "rows": [["1", "Find the digit in the last place you want to keep."], ["2", "Look at the next digit to its right (the 'decider')."], ["3", "5 or more → add 1 to the kept digit. Less than 5 → keep it as it is."], ["4", "Remove all the digits after the kept place."]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Rounding to decimal places", "p": ["10.386 rounded to **1 d.p.**: keep the tenths digit 3; the decider is 8, so round up → **10.4**.", "10.386 rounded to **2 d.p.**: keep the hundredths digit 8; the decider is 6, so round up → **10.39**."], "fig": {"kind": "numline", "min": 10.38, "max": 10.39, "minor": 0, "ticks": [[10.385, "10.385 (halfway)"], [10.39, "10.39"]], "mark": 10.386}, "p2": ["On the number line, 10.386 is past the halfway mark 10.385, so it is nearer 10.39."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Round", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Round 4.6274 to 2 decimal places.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4.63, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [{"v": 4.62, "fb": "The decider 7 is 5 or more, so round up."}, {"v": 4.627, "fb": "That is 3 d.p."}], "bare": true, "hint": "Keep the hundredths digit 2; the decider is 7.", "reason": "4.63."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I round to a number of decimal places?", "p": ["Step 1: Count that many digits after the decimal point; draw a line after the last one.", "Step 2: Look at the digit just after the line.", "Step 3: 5 or more: increase the last kept digit by 1. Under 5: leave it.", "Step 4: Write the answer with exactly that many decimal places – even if the last one is 0."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Rounding to 1 d.p.", "p": [], "q": "Round 27.649 to 1 decimal place.", "steps": [["27.6 | 49", "keep 1 digit after the point"], ["decider is 4", "less than 5"], ["27.6", ""]], "a": "27.6", "check": "27.649 is between 27.6 and 27.7, and below 27.65, so 27.6. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "A 9 that rolls over", "p": [], "q": "Round 3.596 to 2 decimal places.", "steps": [["3.59 | 6", "keep two digits after the point"], ["decider is 6 → add 1 to the 9", ""], ["3.59 + 0.01 = 3.60", "the 9 becomes 0 and carries"], ["3.60", "keep the 0: it shows 2 d.p."]], "a": "3.60", "check": "3.596 lies between 3.59 and 3.60, nearer 3.60. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Rounding money", "p": [], "q": "Three friends share a $25 bill equally. How much should each pay, to the nearest cent?", "steps": [["25 ÷ 3 = 8.3333…", ""], ["cents → 2 d.p.: 8.33 | 33", ""], ["decider 3 → round down", ""], ["$8.33", ""]], "a": "$8.33", "check": "3 × 8.33 = 24.99, 1 cent short – someone pays $8.34. ✓"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Different degrees of accuracy", "p": [], "q": "Round 0.70816 to (a) 1 d.p. (b) 2 d.p. (c) 3 d.p.", "steps": [["1 d.p.: 0.7 | 0816 → decider 0 → 0.7", ""], ["2 d.p.: 0.70 | 816 → decider 8 → 0.71", ""], ["3 d.p.: 0.708 | 16 → decider 1 → 0.708", ""]], "a": "0.7, 0.71, 0.708"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Round up or down?", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m7u03s2t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which number rounds to 5.2 (1 d.p.)?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "Look only at the hundredths digit.", "reason": "5.248 → 5.2.", "options": [{"t": "5.248", "ok": true, "fb": "Decider 4 → stays 5.2."}, {"t": "5.25", "ok": false, "fb": "Decider 5 → 5.3."}, {"t": "5.14", "ok": false, "fb": "That rounds to 5.1."}, {"t": "5.29", "ok": false, "fb": "That rounds to 5.3."}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Looking at the wrong digit", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Round 8.2471 to 1 decimal place.", "lines": ["The last digit is 1, so round down", "8.2471 → 8.247 → 8.25 → 8.3", "Answer: 8.3"], "bad": 0, "why": "Only the digit straight after the kept place matters. Keep 8.2; the decider is 4 → round down. Rounding again and again (8.25 → 8.3) gives the wrong answer.", "fix": [["8.2 | 471: decider is 4", ""], ["Answer: 8.2", ""]], "id": "m7u03s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Rounding in stages", "p": ["Round in ONE step from the original number. 8.2471 → 8.2 (not 8.25 → 8.3)."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Keep the zero", "p": ["3.596 to 2 d.p. is 3.60, not 3.6: the 0 shows the answer is accurate to 2 decimal places."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Find the last digit to keep; look at the next digit (the decider).", "5 or more → round up; under 5 → keep.", "Round in one step from the original number.", "Give exactly the number of decimal places asked for, keeping any final 0."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 840, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "3.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0